{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FuEv8ribvbkJpQqEbHYW7X","type":"tool_result","content":"---VERIFY---\n\"Initial verification read the story, tech design, test plan, implementor package, changed production paths, and TC-5.x tests. Story and epic gates passed, but the production edit path has one blocking validation gap: it accepts messages that are not in a closed turn.\"\n\"messages.edit accepts turnless messages instead of enforcing the closed-turn target boundary\"\n\"Story scope requires messages.edit to validate a closed-turn target (story lines 15-20), and AC-5.1 is scoped to editing a message in a closed turn. In code, readMutableMessage explicitly allows turnStatus null for a gap/no-membership message (packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/internal/store.ts:48-79), and messages.edit only refuses target.turnStatus === 'open' before applying the edit (packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/index.ts:411-434). I verified the production path with an ad hoc runtime scenario: a thread containing only a runtime_note before any prompt produced m1 with no turnId; messages.edit({ messageId: 'm1', content: 'edited gap' }) returned ok:true with changed.messageIds ['m1'] and an empty cascade, and listMessages showed the content mutated. That changes sanctioned record state outside the required closed-turn class.\"\n\"Story Scope: validate target closed turn\"\n\"messages.edit accepts turnless messages instead of enforcing the closed-turn target boundary\"\n\"Story scope requires messages.edit to validate a closed-turn target (story lines 15-20), and AC-5.1 is scoped to editing a message in a closed turn. In code, readMutableMessage explicitly allows turnStatus null for a gap/no-membership message (packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/internal/store.ts:48-79), and messages.edit only refuses target.turnStatus === 'open' before applying the edit (packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/index.ts:411-434). I verified the production path with an ad hoc runtime scenario: a thread containing only a runtime_note before any prompt produced m1 with no turnId; messages.edit({ messageId: 'm1', content: 'edited gap' }) returned ok:true with changed.messageIds ['m1'] and an empty cascade, and listMessages showed the content mutated. That changes sanctioned record state outside the required closed-turn class.\"\n\"Story Scope: validate target closed turn\"\n\"TC-5.1 positive closed-turn edit: packages/lhc/test/mutations.test.ts:141-189 verifies content, blocks, token estimate, cleared/queued result, and rebuild from edited content.\"\n\"Closed-turn-only validation for messages with no turn membership is unmet: the current production path edits them successfully.\"\n\"F-05-001: messages.edit mutates turnless/no-membership messages because null turnStatus is allowed and only open turns are refused.\"","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c1de3f50-133a-4f79-8a5b-672d328b384b","uuid":"04ec94ad-06d5-40b2-a969-9e5207dee022","timestamp":"2026-06-11T06:21:33.351Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"---VERIFY---\n\"Initial verification read the story, tech design, test plan, implementor package, changed production paths, and TC-5.x tests. Story and epic gates passed, but the production edit path has one blocking validation gap: it accepts messages that are not in a closed turn.\"\n\"messages.edit accepts turnless messages instead of enforcing the closed-turn target boundary\"\n\"Story scope requires messages.edit to validate a closed-turn target (story lines 15-20), and AC-5.1 is scoped to editing a message in a closed turn. In code, readMutableMessage explicitly allows turnStatus null for a gap/no-membership message (packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/internal/store.ts:48-79), and messages.edit only refuses target.turnStatus === 'open' before applying the edit (packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/index.ts:411-434). I verified the production path with an ad hoc runtime scenario: a thread containing only a runtime_note before any prompt produced m1 with no turnId; messages.edit({ messageId: 'm1', content: 'edited gap' }) returned ok:true with changed.messageIds ['m1'] and an empty cascade, and listMessages showed the content mutated. That changes sanctioned record state outside the required closed-turn class.\"\n\"Story Scope: validate target closed turn\"\n\"messages.edit accepts turnless messages instead of enforcing the closed-turn target boundary\"\n\"Story scope requires messages.edit to validate a closed-turn target (story lines 15-20), and AC-5.1 is scoped to editing a message in a closed turn. In code, readMutableMessage explicitly allows turnStatus null for a gap/no-membership message (packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/internal/store.ts:48-79), and messages.edit only refuses target.turnStatus === 'open' before applying the edit (packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/index.ts:411-434). I verified the production path with an ad hoc runtime scenario: a thread containing only a runtime_note before any prompt produced m1 with no turnId; messages.edit({ messageId: 'm1', content: 'edited gap' }) returned ok:true with changed.messageIds ['m1'] and an empty cascade, and listMessages showed the content mutated. That changes sanctioned record state outside the required closed-turn class.\"\n\"Story Scope: validate target closed turn\"\n\"TC-5.1 positive closed-turn edit: packages/lhc/test/mutations.test.ts:141-189 verifies content, blocks, token estimate, cleared/queued result, and rebuild from edited content.\"\n\"Closed-turn-only validation for messages with no turn membership is unmet: the current production path edits them successfully.\"\n\"F-05-001: messages.edit mutates turnless/no-membership messages because null turnStatus is allowed and only open turns are refused.\"","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
