{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":980540,"duration_api_ms":957468,"ttft_ms":5464,"ttft_stream_ms":1676,"time_to_request_ms":18,"num_turns":42,"result":"Both gates are fully green: `verify-all` passes (27 files, 218 tests, including the spawned-CLI parity suite).\n\n## Summary\n\nEnforced the closed-turn target boundary for `messages.edit` — the production gap the story verifier flagged as **F-05-001** (turnless messages were silently editable because only open turns were refused).\n\n**Production fix** — `src/domains/messages/index.ts`: generalized the gate from `turnStatus === \"open\"` to `turnStatus !== \"closed\"`. Both failing cases now refuse under the one stable existing code `turn_open`; the reason string branches so the open-turn message reads exactly as before, and a turnless message gets an accurate `\"...has no turn membership; only closed-turn messages can be edited (v1 boundary)\"`. The refusal happens before any record change, so the record is left untouched. I also updated the `edit` doc comment and the `readMutableMessage` view comment in `store.ts` (which previously asserted \"nothing open gates it\" for null membership).\n\n**Test coverage** — `test/mutations.test.ts`: added a turnless refusal case in the **TC-5.5** block alongside the existing open/missing/deleted cases. It seeds a `runtime_note` before any prompt (m1 with `turnId` null, the verifier's exact repro), asserts `ok:false` / `caller_error` / `turn_open`, and asserts the full snapshot (record, forms, queue) is byte-identical after the refusal. It genuinely fails without the production change.\n\n**Manifest** — `test/red-manifest.json`: re-recorded only the `mutations.test.ts` hash via `scripts/record-red-manifest.mjs` (the sanctioned path for the immutability gate), leaving all 24 other entries untouched.\n\n**Preserved** — the closed-turn edit, cascade, `stale_discarded` version-check, and SDK/CLI parity behavior are unchanged: the closed-turn path never hits the new branch, and `verify-all`'s parity suite (closed-turn edit + missing-id refusal) stays green.\n\nOn the error-code choice: I posed it as a question (the request said \"a stable existing story-local error\" without naming one), but since you dismissed it I went with `turn_open` — the boundary's own code, already part of `edit`'s vocabulary — rather than `turn_not_found` (more precise, but a third code) or `message_not_found` (which would falsely claim a visible message doesn't exist). If you'd prefer one of the alternatives, it's a one-line change to the branch plus the test's expected code.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"c1de3f50-133a-4f79-8a5b-672d328b384b","total_cost_usd":2.9548985,"usage":{"input_tokens":3997,"cache_creation_input_tokens":95080,"cache_read_input_tokens":2384009,"output_tokens":31660,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":95080,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":131,"output_tokens":848,"cache_read_input_tokens":110197,"cache_creation_input_tokens":703,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":703},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":514,"outputTokens":19,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.0006090000000000001,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-8":{"inputTokens":3997,"outputTokens":31660,"cacheReadInputTokens":2384009,"cacheCreationInputTokens":95080,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":2.9542895000000002,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[{"tool_name":"AskUserQuestion","tool_use_id":"toolu_01RCUGUxqyEtGiFPhmrYGS32","tool_input":{"questions":[{"question":"A turnless message (exists, but no turn membership) must be refused by messages.edit. Which existing error code should it return?","header":"Refusal code","options":[{"label":"turn_open","description":"Reuse edit's existing turn-state refusal. Treats the boundary as one rule: 'target turn is not closed.' Keeps edit to its current two codes (turn_open / message_not_found). Reason string would say the message isn't in a closed turn rather than 'belongs to open turn'.","preview":"if (target.turnStatus !== \"closed\") {\n  return { ok:false, error:{\n    errorClass:\"caller_error\", code:\"turn_open\",\n    reason: target.turnStatus === \"open\"\n      ? `message ${id} belongs to open turn ${turnId}; ...`\n      : `message ${id} has no turn membership; only closed-turn messages can be edited (v1 boundary)` }};\n}"},{"label":"turn_not_found","description":"Most semantically precise: the message's turn genuinely doesn't exist. Existing epic mutation code (used by turns.delete). Keeps the open-turn case as turn_open and adds a distinct third refusal code to edit.","preview":"if (target.turnStatus === \"open\") { /* turn_open, unchanged */ }\nif (target.turnId === null) {\n  return { ok:false, error:{\n    errorClass:\"caller_error\", code:\"turn_not_found\",\n    reason:`message ${id} has no turn membership; only closed-turn messages can be edited` }};\n}"},{"label":"message_not_found","description":"Treat a turnless message as outside the editable record set, same code as missing/deleted. Simplest, but reports 'not found' for a message the user can plainly see in listMessages — the most misleading of the three.","preview":"// turnless folds into the same code as missing/deleted\ncode: \"message_not_found\"\nreason: `message ${id} is not in a closed turn`"}],"multiSelect":false}]}}],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"873b911d-5c48-4cf3-bcc6-a504aac3deca"}
